---
title: Shakshuka
servings: 2
tags: [middle eastern, vegetarian, weeknight]
cuisine: middle eastern
time: 30 minutes
source: Shakshuka (Middle Eastern Poached or Baked Eggs) by Nagi Maehashi, RecipeTin Eats, https://www.recipetineats.com/shakshuka/
---

If you will finish the eggs in the oven, heat it to 180°C (350°F).

Warm the @olive oil{2%tbsp} in a medium #cast iron skillet{} over medium-high
heat. Cook the @red onion{1}(small, sliced) and @garlic{1%clove}(minced)
~{2%minutes}, until the onion turns translucent.

Add the @red bell pepper{1}(small, in 1/4-inch strips) and cook ~{1%minute}.
Add the @tomato{1}(diced) and cook ~{2%minutes} more, until it collapses into a
paste.

Stir in the @crushed tomatoes{400%g}, @tomato paste{1%tbsp},
@vegetable stock{1/2%cup}(or water), @paprika{1%tsp}, @ground cumin{1%tsp},
@salt{1/2%tsp}, @black pepper{1/4%tsp} and @cayenne{1/4%tsp}.

Turn the heat to medium-low and simmer ~{5%minutes}, until a spoon drawn
through the sauce leaves a trail but it is still loose.

Make four hollows and crack the @eggs{4} into them. Cook ~{1%minute}, until
the edges of the whites turn opaque.

Finish the eggs one of two ways: bake ~{7%minutes} to ~{12%minutes}, or cover
the pan and steam on the stove ~{3%minutes}. Either way, stop while the yolks
still wobble.

Scatter over the @parsley{2%tbsp}(or cilantro, roughly chopped) and serve
straight away with @pita bread{}(or crusty bread).

> Room for six eggs if you want to stretch it to three people.
